        "id": 3438316
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-15T14:27:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Decided to pass both the local sigma and the device sigma, as well as if the device sigma is actually the local sigma, then we only need to do the matrix similarity check for algorithms that rely on device sigma if it is not the same as the local sigma.\n\nAlso made a new function for transforming the local sigma, which makes the local sigma follow the same clamping logic as the device sigma so we get similar behavior when device sigma is large due to high scale factors in the `localToDevice` matrix.",
      "parentUuid": "3cebdab0_aa9f6179",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2023,
        "startChar": 0,
