      "writtenOn": "2026-08-24T14:44:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What could be causing the visual shift is a mismatch with how the LUT is defined and how we\u0027re accessing it. If it is 256 values, it probably stored x\u003d0 into texel 0 but that is sampled as float texel coord \u003d 0.5.  The final value at x\u003d1 into texel 255 is sampled as 255.5.  If we\u0027re not adjusting the normalization range to fit that here, or in how we filled out the table, then it could bias the lookup.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1870,
        "startChar": 33,
        "endLine": 1870,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "cffb4710bf3e1b3f69da0d2d6555f0244f9a3147",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "52fa2768_cb514ea0",
        "filename": "src/sksl/sksl_graphite_frag.sksl",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 1870,
      "author": {
        "id": 3438316
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-15T14:27:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When we generate our CDF LUT, we do store the value of x\u003d0.5 into x\u003d0, so I believe that should be correct when we then sample with x\u003d0.5, we are getting the expected value. This should also be the case with the last pixel where we sample 255.5, which gets clamped to 255, but that is also correct since we stored the value of x\u003d255.5 in pixel 255.",
      "parentUuid": "a240a653_9b9a8844",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1870,
        "startChar": 33,
        "endLine": 1870,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "cffb4710bf3e1b3f69da0d2d6555f0244f9a3147",
